gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":6.357756249093305e-05,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":11.2,"_gate_share_shrink":null,"_gp_share_shrink":null,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.7280580876928957,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.036199998,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":24.1,"_gate_insider_buying":0.778,"_gp_insider_buying":true,"_score_insider_buying":77.8,"pf":[],"description_full":"Netskope, Inc., a cybersecurity company, provides security, networking, and analytics solutions to largest enterprises to mid-sized companies worldwide. The company develops Netskope One platform, a cloud-native platform for securing and accelerating the digital interactions of enterprises. Its platform offers security products comprising cloud inline security, cloud access security broker, data loss prevention, threat protection, secure web gateway, private access, remote browser isolation, Software-as-a-Service (SaaS) security posture management, data security posture management, and enterprise browser solutions for safeguarding human users, non-human entities, and data from cyber threats through the use of zero trust principles. The company's platform also provides networking products, such as Firewall-as-a-Service, internet of things/operational technology intelligence, software-defined wide-area network, dedicated egress IP, and Cloud Packet Stream solutions that enhance performance, resilience, connectivity, and security; and analytics solutions, including advanced analytics, user and entity behavior analytics, data lineage, and digital experience management that enables enterprises with insights into user activity, data movement, and security events across the web, cloud, SaaS, AI applications, private applications, and other environments. Netskope, Inc. was formerly known as Skope, Inc. and changed its name to Netskope, Inc. in November 2012. Netskope, Inc. was incorporated in 2012 and is based in Santa Clara, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Sanjay  Beri | Co-Founder, CEO & Chairman | Age 49 | Compensation: $1.1M (FY2026)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 3K people. Revenue per employee of $216K ranks in the bottom quartile among Technology peers. Each employee generates $5K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $157K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 5\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity).","financial_summary":["Netskope, Inc. is a mid-cap technology business with a $8.9B market cap on $709M of annual revenue.","Gross margins of 68% are the starting point for assessing pricing power.","The business throws off $15M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 2 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","On the balance sheet, interest coverage of 40\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and stock-based comp at 73% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 3.6% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 594% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":5.939074537252192},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.0) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Operating margins 99% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 9.3% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 7% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Elevated sector volatility (38% annualized) adds uncertainty","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Antitrust and platform-regulation risk \u2014 the larger the network effect, the larger the regulatory target on its back, and a single consent decree can reset the moat.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"AI disruption of existing software moats \u2014 incumbents with durable margins face commoditisation as AI-native competitors replicate features at a fraction of the R&D cost.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Valued at a 172% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Insiders are net buyers (78% buy ratio) \u2014 insiders sell for many reasons but buy for only one","Large open-market insider purchases (net $21.6M) \u2014 management putting its own capital behind the business","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"271,770 Shares in Netskope Inc. $NTSK Bought by Lisanti Capital Growth LLC","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/12/271770-shares-in-netskope-inc-ntsk-bought-by-lisanti-capital-growth-llc.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794482234.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.956,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Netskope (NTSK) Gains Momentum as AI Agent Proliferation